Multiplayer 6 (wave 5 NET): each tick's input leaves right after it is captured, one tick per message, in a LAN session; the steps of a
networked match are counted for the log. TransportConnection::FlushOutgoing is the first block of the retail UpdateConnected (which now
calls it: one code path), ReliableSocket::FlushOutgoing runs it for connected connections only (no receives, no callbacks), and
NetworkInputRouter::OnInputCaptured ends with NpLanInputSent (platform/sdk/net/np_lan.cpp), which flushes only in a LAN session with
MSC_LAN_SENDNOW (default 1). np_lan sets the retail tweaks g_nTicksPerPacket (MSC_LAN_TICKS_PER_PACKET, default 1) and s_nPayloadRedundancy
(MSC_LAN_REDUNDANCY, default 6 with one tick per message) when LAN mode starts and restores them when it is left. The single-tick
serialize buffer grows from 200 to 400 bytes (a four-event message is ~229). NetworkInputManager::PrepareUpdate calls NpLanStep (a step,
or a starved step) for the "[mp-lan] net" line. Already in the tree of branch W5NET; the file is the record. See np/docs/wave5-NET.md.

